---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
import { DEMO_COUNT } from '../../lib/demos';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Tools"
  description="Electrochemistry tools that run in your browser: an EIS/DRT analyser for your own impedance data, and a set of bench calculators."
  section="/tools/"
  ogImage="posters/og-tools.png"
>
  <div class="page">
    <article class="prose">
      <span class="overline">Tools</span>
      <h1>Tools</h1>
      <p>
        The <a href={withBase('/demos/')}>demos</a> show how a model behaves. These take your
        numbers and give you something back. Both run entirely in your browser, on the same tested
        code as the demos.
      </p>
    </article>

    <div class="tool-grid">
      <a class="tool-card" href={withBase('/tools/eis/')}>
        <span class="overline">Bring your own data</span>
        <h2>EIS / DRT analyser</h2>
        <p>
          Paste or drop an impedance spectrum. Get Nyquist and Bode plots, the distribution of
          relaxation times, and a table of peaks with each one's resistance, time constant and
          capacitance. Includes a λ sweep so the regularisation choice is something you can see.
        </p>
        <span class="tool-go">open the analyser →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="tool-card" href={withBase('/tools/calculators/')}>
        <span class="overline">Quick numbers</span>
        <h2>Bench calculators</h2>
        <p>
          Debye length, thermal voltage and Nernst slope, Tafel slope, charge-transfer resistance,
          RC time constant, diffusion time, Sand's time, Cottrell current, C-rate, and the
          Bruggeman correction, each with its formula shown.
        </p>
        <span class="tool-go">open the calculators →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="tool-card" href={withBase('/demos/')}>
        <span class="overline">Explore a model</span>
        <h2>{DEMO_COUNT} live demos</h2>
        <p>
          Every demo can export what it plots as CSV or PNG, hold a curve to compare against, and
          copy a link that reopens it with the same settings.
        </p>
        <span class="tool-go">open the demos →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
